  "texts": {
    "preamble": "The Registrar Acharya N.G Ranga ... vs Dr Burla Sunitha Venkata Seshamamba on 21 February, 2024 1 In The High Court Of Andhra Pradesh :: Amaravati (Special Original Jurisdiction) [ 3473 Wednesday ,The ] Aphc010151702023 Twenty First Day Of February Two Thousand And Twenty Four Present The Honourable Sri Justice G.Narendar The Honourable Sri Justice Venuthurumalli Gopala Krishna Rao Writ Appeal No: 436 Of 2023 Between: The Registrar Acharya N.G Ranga Agricultural University Lam And ...Appellant(S) Others And Dr Burla Sunitha Venkata Seshamamba And Others ...Respondent(S) Counsel for the Appellant(s):SRI. Yella Reddy Rajanala (Sc For Angrau) Counsel for the Respondents: Kishore Kumar. A The Court made the following Judgment: 1) Today the learned Counsel for the Appellant University has placed a copy of the proceedings, dated 21.02.2024, bearing Memo No.A2/752/TA/2023-24, whereby the Respondent has been continued as Part -Time Teaching Associate in the Department of Food Safety & Quality Assurance. The Registrar Acharya N.G Ranga ... vs Dr Burla Sunitha Venkata Seshamamba on 21 February, 2024 Indian Kanoon - http://indiankanoon.org/doc/34756760/",
    "facts": "",
    "arguments": "1 2) The learned Counsel for the 1st Respondent would take offence to the use of the words \"hourly basis\" in the second line of the unnumbered second paragraph. 3) The learned Counsel for the Appellants would submit that the 1st Respondent is being paid a consolidated sum of Rs.54,000/- on monthly basis and hence the use of the words \"hourly basis\" is mischievous."
  },
